# Default: store and check out every file byte-for-byte (no LF/CRLF conversion).
* -text

# Data and text sources are stored with LF and always checked out with LF, on every OS
# and regardless of core.autocrlf. data/SHA256SUMS is computed over these LF bytes, so
# `sha256sum -c` (scripts/verify_checksums.sh) passes on Windows, macOS and Linux.
# A file accidentally saved with CRLF is normalised back to LF when it is committed.
data/**/*.csv     text eol=lf
data/**/*.txt     text eol=lf
data/**/*.json    text eol=lf
data/*.md         text eol=lf
data/SHA256SUMS   text eol=lf

# Binary outputs.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
